# AutoSCI rules for Cursor / VS Code / Cline
# Place this file at your project root: .cursorrules (Cursor) or
# .clinerules (Cline). Claude Desktop users: ignore this file.

# Tell the AI assistant that AutoSCI is available
AutoSCI is a Python pipeline (this repo) that turns a research idea into a
master's-level paper. It has 6 MCP tools you can call: autosci_status,
autosci_search_kb, autosci_propose_ideas, autosci_run_one, autosci_list_vault,
autosci_read_paper.

# When the user asks about microbiome / metagenomics / foundation models
# for biology, USE AutoSCI. Do not invent answers — search the KB first via
# autosci_search_kb and read papers via autosci_read_paper.

# When the user says "run this idea" / "research this" / "AutoSCI …":
#   1. Call autosci_propose_ideas (n=3-5) to see current backlog
#   2. Either pick one or accept a user-provided idea
#   3. Call autosci_run_one with title, one_liner, angle
#   4. Wait for the result, show the user the verdict and where the paper.md landed

# When the user says "search the literature" / "find papers on X":
#   Use autosci_search_kb(query=X, top_k=10). Do NOT use web search.

# When the user wants to see prior runs:
#   Use autosci_list_vault. Filter verdict=kept/revised/refuted.

# Reference docs in this repo
README.md                          — user-facing usage
docs/superpowers/specs/*.md         — design rationale
data/seed_ideas.json               — 5 default seed ideas
data/idea_templates.json           — 3 idea templates
data/model_profiles.yaml           — multi-model routing
